  "disclaimer": "Rehearsal assets only. The rehearsal workflow NEVER certifies anything and never emits OVMF_CI_SECURE_BOOT_UKI_PASS; only OVMF_CI_SECURE_BOOT_UKI-CERTIFICATION-workflow.yml may emit the marker - once to stdout and once into the evidence marker file, each time paired with the full nonclaim block - after the complete frozen ceremony succeeds.",
  "enrollment_predicates": "Requirement 5a/5b resolved pre-run as frozen predicates checked in-ceremony by enroll-predicate-check.py (E_ENROLL_*/E_TRUST_*, exit 92): SetupMode==0 && SecureBoot==1, EFI_SUCCESS, BS|RT attributes only; PK/KEK exactly one X509 ESL entry each (owner c501e570-0de0-0001-0000-000000000000, run throwaway DER); sole db exactly the production cert; widened db exactly production+hostile fixture; dbx/dbt/*Default absent; stored data byte-equals the enrolled ESL payloads; per-case VARS byte-equal the run's post-enrollment template (harness allowlist + byte-identity). Post-run VARS image hashes are observational evidence, not pre-frozen expectations. C1' route (ii): the hostile and wrong-signer DER hashes are supplied in-run via C5_HOSTILE_CERT_SHA256 / C5_WRONG_SIGNER_CERT_SHA256 from the per-run GENERATION-RECORD.json (R3 section 15e); the HOSTILE_CERT constant is deleted from enroll-predicate-check.py.",
  "ephemeral": "Throwaway PK/KEK private keys are generated per run inside the prep dir and plain-deleted by run-ceremony.sh (trap EXIT) the moment the enrollment window closes; they are never logged, uploaded or published. The enrolled VARS templates and the enroll FAT images are uploaded as ephemeral public CI artifacts (batch1r3 C7 correction: they are public run data, not secrets). Negative-control fixture keys are generated IN-RUN per ceremony (route (ii), R3 section 15), network-off under /tmp/$PREFIX-*, shredded end-of-step; the historical 2026-09-22 A4 fixture keys were plain-deleted after that regeneration, and the historical fixture BYTES were deleted from the tree in C1' after the 2026-09-24 C2 byte-loss event (R3 section 15d).",
